    "synopsis": {
        "native": "France, la soixantaine, vit seule dans son appartement bourgeois de l\u2019est parisien. Lorsqu\u2019elle entend parler \u00e0 la radio d\u2019une association qui met en contact des personnes r\u00e9fugi\u00e9es sans logement et celles ayant la possibilit\u00e9 de les accueillir, elle d\u00e9croche son t\u00e9l\u00e9phone pour se porter volontaire. Quelques jours plus tard, Reza, jeune afghan d\u2019\u00e0 peine vingt ans, d\u00e9barque dans sa vie. Ces deux \u00eatres, qui n\u2019ont rien en commun, vont devoir apprendre \u00e0 vivre ensemble\u2026",
        "english": "France has been living alone in her apartment since her husband\u2019s death. When she hears on the radio that an NGO is putting in touch homeless migrants and people who are willing to welcome them, she decides, against her family\u2019s opinion to welcome Reza, a young Afghan broken by war and exile. Two worlds meet, and they begin to hold each other\u2019s hands."
    },
